.TH GENRAND 1 "September 2026" "genrand 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
genrand \- generate cryptographically random strings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B genrand
[\fB-hv\fR] [\fIwidth\fR] [\fItype\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B genrand
prints a random string generated from
.I /dev/urandom
followed by a newline.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I width
The length of the string. Defaults to 32. Must be an integer of 1 or higher.
.TP
.I type
The character set for the string. Defaults to
.BR alphanum .
Available values are:
.RS
.TP
.B alphanum
Uppercase letters, lowercase letters, and digits.
.TP
.B lower
Lowercase letters and digits.
.TP
.B mixed
Uppercase letters, lowercase letters, digits, and printable symbols.
.TP
.B numbers
Digits only.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h
Show the help screen.
.TP
.B -v
Show the version number.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Generate the default 32-character alphanumeric string:
.nf
.B genrand
.fi
.TP
Generate a 16-character lowercase string:
.nf
.B genrand 16 lower
.fi
.TP
Generate an 8-digit string:
.nf
.B genrand 8 numbers
.fi
